If the heap has only one element, then that is returned to the calling program. Otherwise,
the top (or 0 index) node is swapped with the bottom (or A.Size - 1 index) node and the
new top node is down-heapified. Note that the “minimum” node is not actually extracted
but allowed to remain in the dArray object A. But, the Size parameter for A is decremented
meaning that the slot that is now occupied by the “minimum” node is viewed as free space
by A. Its content will therefore be overwritten by the next item that is inserted into the
heap.
Finally, let us consider the heapSort method in the next listing.
Heap :: heapSort (){
